  "verbalization": "Betaxolol and Adrb1 are linked through a mechanism involving beta-adrenergic antagonism, as evidenced by their shared pathway through Levobunolol. Betaxolol is implicated in causing Corneal Sensitivity Decreased and Hypoaesthesia Eye, both of which are mediated by Levobunolol, which binds to Adrb1. The presence of a common ancestor in the pathway, Betaxolol and Levobunolol, further supports the notion of a shared mechanism involving beta-adrenergic receptor inhibition. The low final scores in the two paths suggest that while there is a plausible biological link, the evidence is not definitive. The integration of these findings implies that Betaxolol may act as a beta-adrenergic antagonist, potentially modulating Adrb1 activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and therapeutic relevance.",
